<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#lavelua">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lavelua</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lavelua is the title of the paramount king of Uvea, or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wallis-island">Wallis Island</a>, in the Pacific. The kingship emerged from struggles among chiefly lineages after the Tongan conquest of the 15th century. Since the island became part of the French overseas collectivity of Wallis and Futuna, the Lavelua has remained one of its three recognised customary kings, ruling with a council of ministers and district chiefs.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lavelua.jpg" alt="Lavelua" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hobe / Holger Behr · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WF_-Wallis.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
